---
// src/pages/services/microwave-repair/plate-not-rotating.astro
// Wave 4b — failure-mode sub-service under residential microwave pillar.
// SEO: "microwave turntable not spinning", "microwave plate stuck", "turntable motor".
// Lower urgency than other 3 sub-pages: microwave still heats, just creates hot
// spots without rotation. ~25% resolve at $89 dx with re-alignment or coupler.
// $89 residential. BHGS #A49573 + EPA 608 Universal #1346255700410.
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, toE164 } from '../../../data/branches';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../../lib/build-location-array';

const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/services/microwave-repair/plate-not-rotating/";

const title = "Microwave Plate Not Rotating Repair — Same Day";
const description = "Microwave plate not rotating across LA, OC, Ventura. Turntable motor, drive coupler, support roller, alignment. Customer-side checks first. $89 dx.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why won't my microwave plate spin?",
    a: "A microwave plate that won't rotate almost always traces to one of three things: a worn or broken drive coupler (the small plastic clutch on the motor shaft under the plate, year 4 to 7 wear pattern, $20 to $60 part), a failed turntable motor (small synchronous motor under the cavity floor, $200 to $340 replacement), or a plate that's slipped off the coupling tabs or sitting on a cracked support roller. Listen with the door open and the door switch lever pressed (simulates closed): motor humming under the cavity means the motor works and the coupler is broken; silence means the motor itself failed. Drive coupler swap is the cheapest fix at $129 total ($89 dx + $40 part) and we'll talk you through it on the phone before sending a tech if you'd rather DIY."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I fix a microwave turntable that won't turn?",
    a: "Three steps before booking. (1) Lift the plate, rotate it, and set it back down on the three coupling tabs under the center — you'll feel it click into the right position. Misalignment alone stops rotation about 1 in 8 times. (2) Inspect the drive coupler (the small plastic clutch on the motor shaft, dead center under the plate). If it's cracked, slipped off, or missing, replace it — $20 to $60 from a parts supplier, 5 minutes to install. (3) Check the support roller ring (the plastic ring with three wheels that the plate sits on). Cracks or broken wheels stop rotation, $40 to $90 part. If those three don't restore rotation, the turntable motor is the likely cause and we replace it at $200 to $340. $89 residential diagnostic, applied toward repair."
  },
  {
    q: "My microwave plate isn't spinning. Is this dangerous?",
    a: "Not immediately dangerous. The microwave still heats food without rotation, but creates hot spots (some areas overcooked, others undercooked). Worth booking a service call when convenient, but no urgent stop required. Distinct from sparking issues, which are an immediate safety concern, see <a href=\"/services/microwave-repair/sparking-arcing/\">sparking / arcing</a> for that scope."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the cheapest fix?",
    a: "Drive coupler replacement. The drive coupler is the small plastic clutch that connects the motor shaft (under the cavity floor) to the bottom of the glass plate. $20 to $60 part, 5-minute install. Plus $89 diagnostic = $129 total. About year 4 to 7 wear pattern, plastic fatigues from heat cycles. Most common cheap fix on this category."
  },
  {
    q: "Customer-side checks before booking?",
    a: "Three quick checks. (1) Is the plate seated correctly on the coupling? Lift, rotate, set down on the three coupling tabs (you'll feel it click into the right position). (2) Is the drive coupler under the plate snug on the motor shaft, or has it slipped off? (3) Is the support roller ring intact under the plate? Cracks or breaks in the plastic ring stop rotation. About 25% of 'plate not spinning' calls resolve at one of these three steps."
  },
  {
    q: "Turntable motor versus drive coupler, how do you tell which is failing?",
    a: "Listen with the door open and microwave off. Press the door switch lever down with one finger to simulate door closed (some models will spin the motor with door open in this 'paused' state). If you hear the motor humming or spinning under the cavity, the motor is fine and the coupler is broken. If silent, the motor is the failure. Replacement costs differ significantly: coupler $20 to $60, motor $200 to $340."
  },
  {
    q: "My Panasonic NN-SN microwave plate suddenly stopped spinning but heats fine. Motor?",
    a: "Possibly, but Panasonic NN-SN and NN-SD inverter models tie rotation to the control board signal rather than a standalone motor circuit. If the motor tests fine when manually powered, the control board's rotation-control output may have failed. Diagnostic distinguishes between motor failure ($200 to $340) and control board signal issue ($440 to $680). We test motor first, then board."
  },
  {
    q: "A shop quoted me $300 to fix a plate that won't spin — is that fair?",
    a: "Almost never — a drive coupler is a $40 part with a 5-minute install, so the honest charge is $89 diagnostic plus the part, around $129 total, not $300. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair carry common couplers for the top six brands (GE, Whirlpool, Samsung, LG, Panasonic, Sharp) on the van and won't upsell a $200 to $340 turntable motor when the cheap coupler is the actual fix. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you keep turntable parts on the truck so this gets fixed same visit?",
    a: "Yes — our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair stock drive couplers and generic-spec turntable motors for GE, Whirlpool, Samsung, LG, Panasonic, and Sharp, so most plate-not-spinning jobs finish on the first visit. A coupler runs about $129 total and a turntable motor $200 to $340; only inverter control-board issues need a follow-up order. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty?",
    a: "90 days parts and labor on every repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

const schemaJsons = [
